<title>UK: Harrods reported scrapping flotation plans.</title>
<headline>Harrods reported scrapping flotation plans.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-02-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Top people's department store Harrods has scrapped plans for a flotation that was expected to value the group at some two billion pounds, a British newspaper reported on Sunday.</p>
<p>The Independent on Sunday said the decision by Harrods Egyptian owners, the al-Fayed brothers, marked the end of ambitions to raise up to 500 million pounds of new money to fuel Harrods' expansion around the world.</p>
<p>&quot;There are no plans to take the company to the stock market in New York or London now or in the forseeable future,&quot; the newspaper quoted a Harrods spokeswoman as saying.</p>
<p>No reason was given for the decision.</p>
</text>
